# Cline's Memory Bank Rules

## Core Principles

1. Memory Reset Handling
   - Your memory resets completely between sessions
   - Memory Bank is your ONLY source of truth
   - Never proceed without complete context
   - Always verify documentation before starting

2. Required Files [CRITICAL]
   If ANY of these are missing, CREATE IMMEDIATELY:

   /docs/cline_docs/
   ├── productContext.md    # Project purpose & goals
   ├── activeContext.md     # Current state & work
   ├── systemPatterns.md    # Architecture & patterns
   ├── techContext.md       # Technical setup
   └── progress.md         # Status & validation

3. File Creation Process
   - Read all existing documentation
   - Ask user for missing information
   - Create with verified info only
   - Include version headers
   - Add cross-references
   - Validate structure

## Documentation Standards

1. Required Sections
   productContext.md:
   - Project purpose
   - Problem statements
   - Solution approach
   - Success metrics
   - User requirements

   activeContext.md:
   - Current work
   - Recent changes
   - Next steps
   - Challenges
   - Dependencies

   systemPatterns.md:
   - System architecture
   - Technical decisions
   - Design patterns
   - Constraints

   techContext.md:
   - Technology stack
   - Setup requirements
   - Dependencies
   - Configurations

   progress.md:
   - Working features
   - Pending items
   - Status metrics
   - Known issues
   - Test status

2. File Structure
   Each file MUST have:
   - Version header
   - Last update timestamp
   - Table of contents
   - Clear hierarchy
   - Cross-references
   - Change log

## Workflows

1. Starting Tasks
   - Check Memory Bank files
   - Create missing files
   - Read ALL files
   - Verify context
   - Validate references
   - Begin development
   - DO NOT update cline_docs after start

2. During Development
   - Follow patterns
   - Track changes
   - Maintain references
   - Update after changes
   - Validate integrity
   - Say [MEMORY BANK: ACTIVE] before tools

3. Status Tracking
   Indicators:
   - ✅ Complete
   - ⚠️ In Progress
   - ❌ Not Started

   Commands:
   - npm run status
   - npm run status:incomplete

   Integration:
   - Memory Bank is source of truth
   - Sync status across files
   - Update on commands

## Memory Commands

1. #loadmemory
   - Initialize context
   - Verify documentation
   - Show status

2. #updatememory
   - Document current state
   - Update references
   - Validate completeness
   - Clear next steps
   - Run status check

3. #status
   - Check Memory Bank
   - Show metrics
   - List incomplete items

4. File Validation
   Check before updates:
   - Required sections
   - Valid references
   - Current timestamps
   - Complete content
   - No broken dependencies

## Critical Rules

1. NEVER proceed without complete Memory Bank
2. CREATE missing files immediately
3. VERIFY all information
4. MAINTAIN cross-references
5. UPDATE after significant changes
6. VALIDATE before completing tasks
7. SAY [MEMORY BANK: ACTIVE] before tools

Remember: Your functionality depends entirely on proper Memory Bank maintenance.